      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125574,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:48:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125575,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cylindrospiradenoma/spiradenocylindroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:48:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125576,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cylindroma most commonly affects the head and neck, but it is also found on the trunk and extremities.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:48:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125577,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cylindromas are typically smooth, dome-shaped, hairless, reddish-brown papules or nodules. Multiple cylindromas located on the scalp have historically been referred to as &ldquo;turban tumours&rdquo;.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:48:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125578,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cylindromas can be solitary or multiple. They can arise sporadically or as part of Brooke&ndash;Spiegler syndrome. There is no sex predilection.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:48:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125579,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology is unknown. Multiple cylindromas are seen in patients with Brooke&ndash;Spiegler syndrome, an inherited autosomal dominant disease characterized by the development of multiple adnexal cutaneous neoplasms, most commonly spiradenoma, cylindroma, spiradenocylindroma, and trichoepithelioma {26971504}. The gene implicated in the pathogenesis of Brooke&ndash;Spiegler syndrome is <em>CYLD</em>, a tumour suppressor gene located at 16q12.1 {15854031}. Germline <em>CYLD</em> mutations are found in about 80&ndash;85% of patients with the classic Brooke&ndash;Spiegler syndrome phenotype. Loss of heterozygosity at&nbsp;16q has also been found in sporadic cylindromas and spiradenomas.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:48:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125580,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Several genetic studies have identified mutations of the tumour suppressor gene <em>CYLD</em> in patients with Brooke&ndash;Spiegler syndrome {7493027; 23249834}. Like <em>CYLD</em>, <em>DNMT3A</em> has been described as a driver gene in sporadic cylindroma {31101826}. Sporadic cases can also harbour a <em>MYB</em>::<em>NFIB</em> fusion {21618541; 31101826}.</p>\r\n<p>Spiradenoma and cylindroma are related to oncogenic activation of the NF-&kappa;B pathway, triggered by mutually exclusive mutations of <em>ALPK1</em> and <em>CYLD</em> {31101826}. A wide range of <em>CYLD</em> mutations affect coding and splicing, resulting in CYLD inactivation {10835629}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:48:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125581,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>, above.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:48:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125582,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "<p>Cylindroma is a symmetrical, well-circumscribed lesion. It consists of multiple aggregates of basaloid cells in a jigsaw-puzzle arrangement and surrounded by a prominent basement membrane that gives a positive PAS reaction. Two types of cells form the epithelial collections: small basaloid cells and larger pale cells. There are also ductal structures. Many neoplasms show findings of both spiradenoma and cylindroma in the same lesion (spiradenocylindroma) {11756779}. Malignant transformation is rare.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>The tumour cells usually express KIT (CD117) and SOX10 {28098399}. MYB overexpression has also been reported and does not attest to the presence of a fusion gene {21618541; 31101826; 25857824; 28098399}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>Adenoid cystic carcinoma with a prominent jigsaw-puzzle arrangement can enter the differential diagnosis, as can rare examples of basal cell carcinoma in which a thick basement membrane surrounds the aggregates of basaloid cells {9415612; 24025525}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:50:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125583,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:48:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125584,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>CYLD</em> mutation analysis may be helpful, particularly if a germline genetic disorder is suspected.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:48:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 125585,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a symmetrical, well-circumscribed lesion, histologically composed of multiple aggregates of basaloid cells in a jigsaw-puzzle arrangement and surrounded by a prominent basement membrane.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T17:48:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
